.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.DS_Store
dist/
*.egg-info/
# .claude/ holds BOTH shared project context and personal local state.
# The skills and the reviewer agent are part of the repo — a clone without
# them gets a different reviewer and different contracts. settings.local.json
# is per-developer (accumulated permission grants) and stays out.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/
.cle/
# Scratch state directories. `full_loop.sh` defaults to `.cle-demo`, and
# `run_state.py` to `.cle-r36-<corpus>`; both are throwaway by construction and
# neither should ever be indexed. `.cle/` alone did not cover them.
.cle-*/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docs/RESUME.md
temp_run.md

# Agent YAMLs are REGENERATED by examples/make_fixture.py on every demo run
# (full_loop.sh step 1, the dashboard init, the README quick start). No test
# reads them from disk, so tracking them would only dirty the tree each run.
# The prompt_history*.jsonl artifacts stay TRACKED on purpose: the adversarial
# test consumes the committed data, not the generator.
examples/*_agent.yaml

# ── Corpus artifacts (R34 task 0, security gate) ────────────────────────────
# `examples/bigquery/data/` holds 2.3 GB of WildChat material: 1.37M real user
# prompts (wildchat_cohort_turns), 86 shard chunks, and an identity file with
# hashed_ip + country + language for 3.2M conversations. WildChat is prompts
# consented for RESEARCH; redistributing them from a public repository is not a
# decision this project gets to make. Stack Overflow material is public, but it
# is derived data that any run regenerates, so it is ignored on the same rule
# rather than carved out — a narrower rule is one more thing to get right.
#
# Nothing here was ever committed. The exposure was that a single `git add -A`
# would have indexed all of it.
examples/bigquery/data/

# R36 task 0.b — the same exposure, one directory over. `prepare_states.py`
# writes the CLI-shaped histories next to the corpus, not inside it, so the
# rule above did not reach them: `history_wildchat.jsonl` is 3.5 Mo of raw
# WildChat prompts, untracked and NOT ignored. R34's own audit had certified
# this area clean by listing `examples/bigquery/data/` and stopping there.
#
# The whole directory goes, not just the WildChat file: these are generated
# states that `prepare_states.py` reproduces, and a rule that enumerates the
# private one is a rule that misses the next one.
examples/bigquery/states/

# R36 task 1.b — probe fixtures, GENERATED, not corpus.
# `make_multiuser.py` partitions the synthetic GDG corpus into N users, one
# oplog each (R25 task 0, R26 tasks 1a-1c). 68 files, 4.8 Mo, all reproducible
# by rerunning that script. Committing them would be committing the output of a
# committed generator.
#
# The five hand-built fixtures stay tracked and are NOT matched by these globs:
# prompt_history.jsonl, prompt_history_adversarial.jsonl, prompt_history_gdg.jsonl,
# prompt_history_holdout.jsonl, gdg_ground_truth.json.
examples/sw[0-9]*_user*.jsonl
examples/sw[0-9]*_manifest.json
examples/ph[0-9]*_user*.jsonl
examples/ph[0-9]*_manifest.json
examples/prompt_history_user[0-9]*.jsonl
examples/prompt_history_manifest.json

# R36 — working files, not deliverables.
# The run journals record how each measurement was obtained; the published
# figures already carry their reproduction command (docs/FINDINGS.md), so a
# reader reproduces the result instead of reading how it was reached.
# PRESERVED.md is a transit file for content awaiting a decision.
temp_run_*.md
temp_commits*.sh
PRESERVED.md

# `docs/VALIDATION.md` is a snapshot of one validation pass: a commit hash, a
# date, a `.cle` digest, a guard ratio, a suite count. Every one of those is
# stale the next time anything changes, and a document that says "verified" while
# describing a tree that no longer exists is worse than no document.
#
# What was durable in it has been moved into files that are maintained: the
# frozen defects are pinned by `tests/unit/test_frozen_defects.py` and go red the
# day they are fixed, and the two limits nothing else stated (no ground truth for
# demotion, level 2 does not exist) now live in `docs/FINDINGS.md`.
#
# Regenerate it for a given pass if you want one; do not ship it.
docs/VALIDATION.md
